1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:04,840
Episode 13

2
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:04,840
Episode 13

3
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:04,840
The Misanthrope and the Nigh Future

4
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:04,840
The Misanthrope and the Nigh Future

5
00:00:02,030 --> 00:00:04,170
Uchami, what's that?

6
00:00:04,170 --> 00:00:05,190
A piece of straw.

7
00:00:05,630 --> 00:00:08,610
My assignment is 
to use this to trade with.

8
00:00:08,610 --> 00:00:12,470
Like the tale of the Straw Millionaire?

9
00:00:12,470 --> 00:00:13,540
That's right.

10
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:17,090
At the end, I'll need to trade 
for something with the principal.

11
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:19,940
What's your assignment, Maki?

12
00:00:20,270 --> 00:00:22,340
As for me...

13
00:00:22,660 --> 00:00:26,800
I need to find a hundred truths.

14
00:00:26,800 --> 00:00:29,400
And write them down in this tiny book.

15
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:33,710
My assignment is getting 5,000 
followers on social media!

16
00:00:33,710 --> 00:00:37,080
But how exactly do I gain followers?

17
00:00:37,630 --> 00:00:40,080
Think about how you can 
show empathy for others.

18
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:44,420
Ms. Mirai, do you know 
a lot about social media?

19
00:00:45,650 --> 00:00:48,630
I have 124,000 followers!

20
00:00:48,630 --> 00:00:50,280
That's amazing!

21
00:00:50,280 --> 00:00:53,620
Ms. Mirai, could you please 
teach me your secrets?

22
00:00:53,620 --> 00:00:54,720
Of course!

23
00:00:55,260 --> 00:00:57,550
Wakaba, what's your assignment?

24
00:00:57,550 --> 00:00:59,310
Mine is to keep a diary.

25
00:00:59,630 --> 00:01:03,190
I need to write at least three things 
that happen every day in it.

26
00:01:03,440 --> 00:01:06,870
Mine is making dinners for the dorm!

27
00:01:06,870 --> 00:01:09,050
Nezu, you know how to cook?

28
00:01:10,670 --> 00:01:12,390
Technically speaking...

29
00:01:13,450 --> 00:01:16,020
Your choice of words speaks volumes.

30
00:01:16,430 --> 00:01:21,140
You know how cooking ingredients 
taste fine the way they are?

31
00:01:21,140 --> 00:01:22,450
So, well...

32
00:01:22,450 --> 00:01:24,570
I see, so you sneak in some bites.

33
00:01:25,110 --> 00:01:27,510
Tobari, what's your assignment?

34
00:01:27,510 --> 00:01:33,870
I have to compose a song using at least
 three instruments I've never played.

35
00:01:33,870 --> 00:01:36,520
Another task on the creative side, huh?

36
00:01:36,520 --> 00:01:37,910
Pretty much.

37
00:01:37,910 --> 00:01:40,920
Okay, your assignments have just begun.

38
00:01:41,340 --> 00:01:45,630
Don't panic and tackle them 
at a measured and steady pace.

39
00:01:45,940 --> 00:01:46,840
Understood?

40
00:01:46,840 --> 00:01:48,330
Yes!

41
00:01:51,030 --> 00:01:53,080
Mr. Hitoma, I'm done!

42
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:53,930
That was fast!

43
00:01:54,530 --> 00:01:58,350
What instruments did you use 
that you've never played?

44
00:01:58,780 --> 00:02:02,440
The kazoo, the daxophone, 
and the wheelharp!

45
00:02:02,440 --> 00:02:04,610
I don't recognize a single one...

46
00:02:04,860 --> 00:02:08,320
They produce pretty 
interesting sounds. Wanna hear?

47
00:02:08,770 --> 00:02:10,030
Oh? Let's see.

48
00:02:10,030 --> 00:02:11,890
Tobari, that's not <i>fair</i>!

49
00:02:11,890 --> 00:02:14,560
Sharing earbuds with Mr. Rei!

50
00:02:14,560 --> 00:02:17,240
I want him to ask me 
about my assignment, too!

51
00:02:17,790 --> 00:02:20,930
Oh, how's yours going, Ryuzaki?

52
00:02:20,930 --> 00:02:24,100
I'm not getting any followers at all.

53
00:02:24,470 --> 00:02:29,480
If you ask me, gaining followers is all 
about getting people to like you.

54
00:02:29,480 --> 00:02:34,340
I'm fine with Mr. Rei being 
the only person who likes me.

55
00:02:34,340 --> 00:02:37,330
Then you won't be able to 
complete your assignment.

56
00:02:37,330 --> 00:02:42,480
Why don't you try using your 
strengths to draw people in?

57
00:02:42,480 --> 00:02:44,980
Ryuzaki, what do you 
think your strengths are?

58
00:02:44,980 --> 00:02:47,850
How much I love you, Mr. Rei!

59
00:02:48,450 --> 00:02:49,870
No, not what I mean.

60
00:02:50,610 --> 00:02:53,570
I like it! Why don't you try that out?

61
00:02:53,570 --> 00:02:54,660
Be serious.

62
00:02:54,660 --> 00:02:59,460
So you mean posting my daily 
fantasies about Mr. Rei?

63
00:02:59,460 --> 00:03:01,500
Sounds awesome!

64
00:03:02,070 --> 00:03:03,960
Take a look at my assignment, too.

65
00:03:04,420 --> 00:03:06,380
How are your Straw 
Millionaire trades going?

66
00:03:06,730 --> 00:03:11,010
I traded Maki's pen for a photo of Aoi,

67
00:03:11,010 --> 00:03:15,320
which I traded with Konno 
from the Aoi Fan Club for some snacks,

68
00:03:15,320 --> 00:03:18,340
which I traded with Machi 
for her school notebook,

69
00:03:18,340 --> 00:03:20,930
which I traded with Yuki for some makeup,

70
00:03:22,170 --> 00:03:25,190
which I traded with 
Karin for a magic stone.

71
00:03:25,190 --> 00:03:28,010
What's a magic stone?

72
00:03:28,010 --> 00:03:30,730
It's like a piggy bank for magical power.

73
00:03:32,150 --> 00:03:36,400
But no one wants to trade 
for this magic stone.

74
00:03:36,400 --> 00:03:40,320
At this rate, I'll end up handing 
this rock in to the principal.

75
00:03:40,320 --> 00:03:42,570
You're not handing it in yet?

76
00:03:42,570 --> 00:03:44,750
I'll wait until just before the deadline.

77
00:03:45,430 --> 00:03:48,950
If I trade it for something better, 
I can get a better grade.

78
00:03:49,890 --> 00:03:52,090
Oh yeah, how are you doing, Nezu?

79
00:03:53,180 --> 00:03:55,820
It's looking dicey, 
but I'm trying my best.

80
00:03:55,820 --> 00:03:57,230
Dicey?

81
00:03:57,230 --> 00:04:01,470
I'm only allowed to taste 
a teaspoon's worth as I cook.

82
00:04:02,310 --> 00:04:04,750
After tasting a teaspoon...

83
00:04:05,090 --> 00:04:09,910
I want more and more, 
and get withdrawal symptoms...

84
00:04:09,910 --> 00:04:14,280
I even get visions of me stuffing my face!

85
00:04:13,320 --> 00:04:14,280
It's <i>that</i> bad?!

86
00:04:14,680 --> 00:04:17,050
Wakaba, your assignment was a diary?

87
00:04:17,050 --> 00:04:18,360
How's that going?

88
00:04:18,360 --> 00:04:19,770
Quite smoothly.

89
00:04:20,310 --> 00:04:24,090
Since I have to write down three things 
that happen every day,

90
00:04:24,410 --> 00:04:26,370
I've learned a lot from it as well.

91
00:04:26,630 --> 00:04:28,770
In what ways?

92
00:04:28,770 --> 00:04:34,590
It's made me interact 
with others more, just like I am now.

93
00:04:34,940 --> 00:04:37,630
Mr. Hitoma, I did it!

94
00:04:38,030 --> 00:04:42,890
Okonogi, you had to find a hundred truths.

95
00:04:43,330 --> 00:04:44,910
"The sky is blue."

96
00:04:47,130 --> 00:04:48,440
"Clouds are white."

97
00:04:49,410 --> 00:04:51,930
"This is the thirty-second entry."

98
00:04:53,220 --> 00:04:55,350
"This is the thirty-third."

99
00:04:56,070 --> 00:04:57,370
Okonogi.

100
00:04:57,370 --> 00:04:58,360
Huh?

101
00:04:58,810 --> 00:05:00,810
Give me a second here.

102
00:05:01,960 --> 00:05:04,170
Let me figure out 
everything I want to say.

103
00:05:04,170 --> 00:05:11,380
In my opinion, "finding" here 
means making new discoveries.

104
00:05:11,620 --> 00:05:13,500
Discoveries?

105
00:05:14,020 --> 00:05:16,870
Are there a hundred discoveries in here?

106
00:05:16,870 --> 00:05:18,620
Sure are!

107
00:05:20,130 --> 00:05:23,800
Okonogi, you like cute things, don't you?

108
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:24,980
Yeah!

109
00:05:24,980 --> 00:05:28,250
I love everything that's adorbs!

110
00:05:28,250 --> 00:05:30,780
And is that the truth?

111
00:05:30,780 --> 00:05:33,230
Huh? Hmph!

112
00:05:33,450 --> 00:05:35,900
Would you call what 
you wrote down cute?

113
00:05:37,310 --> 00:05:40,510
I-It's not adorbs...

114
00:05:40,510 --> 00:05:42,470
So this entry?

115
00:05:43,260 --> 00:05:46,410
It's not the truth...

116
00:05:46,910 --> 00:05:49,620
I hate to say this 
after everything you wrote,

117
00:05:49,620 --> 00:05:53,460
but can you find another 
hundred truths for me?

118
00:05:55,030 --> 00:05:57,610
I'll do my best...

119
00:06:01,740 --> 00:06:03,800
Mr. Hitoma!

120
00:06:05,220 --> 00:06:08,390
Look, look! I filled it out!

121
00:06:08,710 --> 00:06:09,930
Let's see...

122
00:06:11,800 --> 00:06:14,310
"Macchi's cooking is tasty."

123
00:06:14,550 --> 00:06:16,770
"Tobarin has pretty eyes."

124
00:06:17,420 --> 00:06:19,810
"Prince Waka is cute when she smiles."

125
00:06:20,460 --> 00:06:23,640
"Karin loves Mr. Hitoma."

126
00:06:24,190 --> 00:06:26,990
"Ushami is a hard worker."

127
00:06:26,990 --> 00:06:28,950
"I love my mom."

128
00:06:29,590 --> 00:06:31,150
Oh, there you go.

129
00:06:31,150 --> 00:06:34,910
Do you think these are cutie-cute?

130
00:06:34,910 --> 00:06:39,300
I can tell you really 
think these are true.

131
00:06:39,300 --> 00:06:42,970
Yeah, but are they cutie-cute?

132
00:06:42,970 --> 00:06:45,140
Huh? They're...

133
00:06:45,140 --> 00:06:46,860
They're?

134
00:06:47,590 --> 00:06:51,430
They're cutieâ€”I mean, cute.

135
00:06:52,930 --> 00:06:54,660
Thanks!

136
00:06:57,780 --> 00:06:59,510
She's amazing.

137
00:06:59,510 --> 00:07:01,470
Amazing how?

138
00:07:01,470 --> 00:07:02,570
Um...

139
00:07:02,570 --> 00:07:04,990
I mean, it's your fault!

140
00:07:05,820 --> 00:07:08,140
I don't wanna hear that from you!

141
00:07:08,530 --> 00:07:09,160
Let's go.

142
00:07:09,160 --> 00:07:10,200
Yes!

143
00:07:12,370 --> 00:07:15,060
What's going on, you two?

144
00:07:15,060 --> 00:07:16,820
Ugh! It's Usami!

145
00:07:16,820 --> 00:07:19,320
Tsukino, you've got some nerve informally

146
00:07:19,320 --> 00:07:22,380
calling me by my last name
as a beginner class student.

147
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:25,470
It's not my fault! 
Maibara's the one who...

148
00:07:25,470 --> 00:07:26,700
What happened?

149
00:07:27,650 --> 00:07:28,770
Hitoma.

150
00:07:28,770 --> 00:07:31,160
Can you tell us what this is about?

151
00:07:31,380 --> 00:07:35,580
The two of us are a pair for our 
group assignment to move up a grade.

152
00:07:35,580 --> 00:07:39,060
We need to do ten things that 
make people tell us, "Thank you."

153
00:07:39,390 --> 00:07:41,850
But Maibara wants out of the group!

154
00:07:41,850 --> 00:07:43,210
I didn't say that!

155
00:07:43,210 --> 00:07:46,450
I said I can't go along 
with what you're doing!

156
00:07:46,450 --> 00:07:47,970
That's the same thing!

157
00:07:47,970 --> 00:07:50,680
Hey, hold on. Let's calm down.

158
00:07:51,510 --> 00:07:53,650
Why can't you go along with her?

159
00:07:55,160 --> 00:07:58,480
It's not right to cause trouble 
for someone in order to help them.

160
00:07:58,480 --> 00:07:59,770
What?

161
00:07:59,770 --> 00:08:02,170
It fulfills the assignment, doesn't it?!

162
00:08:02,170 --> 00:08:05,820
You're not supposed to hide someone's 
stuff so you can lend them your own!

163
00:08:06,660 --> 00:08:09,900
I agree. I don't think that's right.

164
00:08:09,900 --> 00:08:11,470
I feel the same way.

165
00:08:13,640 --> 00:08:14,890
What?

166
00:08:14,890 --> 00:08:17,180
If you've got something 
to say, out with it.

167
00:08:17,180 --> 00:08:19,990
Usami, don't be too harsh on her.

168
00:08:21,220 --> 00:08:22,450
Why me?

169
00:08:22,990 --> 00:08:27,740
I was just trying 
to finish our assignment...

170
00:08:28,730 --> 00:08:33,080
But I think it was wrong 
to hide people's belongings.

171
00:08:37,710 --> 00:08:38,850
Wait up!

172
00:09:04,410 --> 00:09:05,540
Are you all right?!

173
00:09:05,540 --> 00:09:06,410
What?

174
00:09:06,410 --> 00:09:08,330
Are you hurt at all?!

175
00:09:09,660 --> 00:09:12,510
No, I'm fine.

176
00:09:13,350 --> 00:09:15,010
That's good to hear.

177
00:09:15,010 --> 00:09:16,890
It's not good at all!

178
00:09:16,890 --> 00:09:19,070
Your graduation assignment!

179
00:09:19,400 --> 00:09:21,410
Don't worry about that.

180
00:09:21,410 --> 00:09:23,210
But because of me...

181
00:09:23,210 --> 00:09:25,950
It's more important 
that you didn't get hurt.

182
00:09:25,950 --> 00:09:26,730
Still!

183
00:09:26,730 --> 00:09:28,280
Listen to me!

184
00:09:30,200 --> 00:09:33,410
I'm not so petty as to let 
that get me down.

185
00:09:33,910 --> 00:09:36,650
I'm a lot more serious 
than that about being here.

186
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:38,910
Show a little more respect.

187
00:09:38,910 --> 00:09:43,050
I'll start over from scratch, 
no matter how many times it may take.

188
00:09:43,050 --> 00:09:47,340
So let me see you start over as well!

189
00:09:49,430 --> 00:09:51,150
I'm sorry...

190
00:09:51,990 --> 00:09:53,720
I'll do my best...

191
00:09:54,470 --> 00:09:57,050
I swear it!

192
00:10:01,880 --> 00:10:04,600
Tell that to Inaho, not me.

193
00:10:07,690 --> 00:10:09,540
I'm sorry, too.

194
00:10:10,010 --> 00:10:13,390
I had made you do everything.

195
00:10:14,810 --> 00:10:15,940
Sorry.

196
00:10:16,450 --> 00:10:20,050
I'm sorry, too.

197
00:10:23,080 --> 00:10:24,330
Hitoma.

198
00:10:24,330 --> 00:10:27,270
Looks like that rock 
released its power on its own.

199
00:10:27,730 --> 00:10:30,230
Does that count as unhuman-like behavior?

200
00:10:30,740 --> 00:10:33,910
It was out of your hands, 
so I think we'd overlook it...

201
00:10:35,030 --> 00:10:36,890
I'll ask just to be safe.

202
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:44,120
I thought this would be 
the year Usami graduated for sure...

203
00:10:44,770 --> 00:10:48,310
But the item for her assignment is gone.

204
00:10:49,570 --> 00:10:50,730
Mr. Hitoma!

205
00:10:55,990 --> 00:10:58,910
Congratulations!

206
00:10:59,850 --> 00:11:02,050
What's this all about, Principal?!

207
00:11:02,050 --> 00:11:03,970
I forgot to tell you.

208
00:11:04,350 --> 00:11:07,330
This is what it's like whenever 
we have someone graduating.

209
00:11:07,630 --> 00:11:11,750
Good work on your graduation 
assignments, everyone!

210
00:11:11,750 --> 00:11:18,300
After careful consideration, we've decided
on this year's graduates!

211
00:11:19,550 --> 00:11:22,720
We will have one student 
graduating this year.

212
00:11:23,030 --> 00:11:28,160
She's been harder on herself 
than anyone else,

213
00:11:28,160 --> 00:11:33,190
facing her goals head-on while diligently 
studying and striving all this time.

214
00:11:34,550 --> 00:11:38,350
Despite her tendency 
to be just as strict on others,

215
00:11:38,350 --> 00:11:44,990
she has fostered her sense of caring to
become a student who cherishes others.

216
00:11:45,730 --> 00:11:48,610
For these reasons stated...

217
00:11:48,610 --> 00:11:52,840
Sui Usami. You are this year's...

218
00:11:52,840 --> 00:11:54,930
That can't be right!

219
00:11:54,930 --> 00:11:57,800
I never handed in my 
graduation assignment!

220
00:11:58,230 --> 00:12:02,300
So... this must be some sort of mistake.

221
00:12:02,300 --> 00:12:05,970
No, this is no mistake.

222
00:12:06,280 --> 00:12:10,200
Then what? I don't need you 
to make an exception for me.

223
00:12:10,200 --> 00:12:11,900
That doesn't make me happy!

224
00:12:12,120 --> 00:12:15,640
We received an assignment submission.

225
00:12:16,130 --> 00:12:19,070
An appeal letter, that is.

226
00:12:19,380 --> 00:12:20,850
An appeal letter?

227
00:12:21,190 --> 00:12:24,000
Asking for Sui Usami's 
graduation assignment

228
00:12:24,000 --> 00:12:26,530
to be considered complete.

229
00:12:26,530 --> 00:12:31,370
Written by Tsukino Wakuma 
from the beginner class.

230
00:12:31,990 --> 00:12:34,290
It says she wants to repay 
the kindness you've shown.

231
00:12:34,290 --> 00:12:35,790
Repay me?

232
00:12:36,290 --> 00:12:38,950
To give something back 
for what you've done.

233
00:12:39,370 --> 00:12:41,710
As part of the trade 
for the piece of straw.

234
00:12:42,270 --> 00:12:45,220
That's just a made-up rationale.

235
00:12:45,220 --> 00:12:46,590
Repaying kindness.

236
00:12:47,720 --> 00:12:49,940
That's what you've always talked about.

237
00:12:51,470 --> 00:12:57,240
Your reason at first to become human was 
to repay the kindness a human showed you.

238
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:02,450
Didn't you teach her how to write those 
words for your assignment last year?

239
00:13:03,290 --> 00:13:08,580
And so, this is the final trade.

240
00:13:09,110 --> 00:13:11,500
A ring...

241
00:13:11,870 --> 00:13:14,280
Based on this evaluation...

242
00:13:14,280 --> 00:13:15,950
Sui Usami.

243
00:13:15,950 --> 00:13:19,960
You are this year's graduating student!

244
00:13:21,810 --> 00:13:23,720
Congratulations, Usami.

245
00:13:24,760 --> 00:13:26,510
You can get in touch with this.

246
00:13:27,500 --> 00:13:29,550
Is now the time for that?

247
00:13:29,550 --> 00:13:34,230
But well, I guess I can contact 
you once in a while, Hitoma.

248
00:13:34,230 --> 00:13:37,410
This is Sae's card, not mine.

249
00:13:37,410 --> 00:13:40,620
Sae's? Tell me that sooner!

250
00:13:40,620 --> 00:13:43,910
Didn't I promise to hold onto it 
until you graduated?

251
00:13:48,190 --> 00:13:52,250
I can't wait to see what 
that brat is like all grown up.

252
00:13:53,370 --> 00:13:54,260
Hitoma.

253
00:13:54,890 --> 00:13:57,960
One day, I'll repay your kindness as well.

254
00:13:58,270 --> 00:14:01,380
So make sure you stay healthy until then.

255
00:14:02,050 --> 00:14:02,770
Sure.

256
00:14:05,190 --> 00:14:08,200
We have one student graduating this year.

257
00:14:08,200 --> 00:14:09,430
Yeah.

258
00:14:09,430 --> 00:14:11,850
But there are still five students 
in the advanced class,

259
00:14:12,690 --> 00:14:14,740
as well as any students 
who move up next year...

260
00:14:15,620 --> 00:14:16,650
Hitoma.

261
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:18,260
Usami.

262
00:14:18,260 --> 00:14:20,710
There's something I need to say to you.

263
00:14:21,560 --> 00:14:27,570
I enrolled here to become human 
and repay Seiko.

264
00:14:28,130 --> 00:14:34,070
Because of that, I couldn't 
spend Seiko's last days with her.

265
00:14:35,220 --> 00:14:36,520
That's right.

266
00:14:36,890 --> 00:14:39,150
I'd regretted it.

267
00:14:40,270 --> 00:14:45,930
All this time, I regretted 
not staying with Seiko.

268
00:14:46,220 --> 00:14:47,170
I see...

269
00:14:47,750 --> 00:14:52,790
But thanks to you, I managed 
to meet Seiko before she left us.

270
00:14:54,060 --> 00:14:59,010
I found a new purpose, 
and now I can meet Sae as an adult.

271
00:14:59,590 --> 00:15:00,340
Yeah.

272
00:15:01,160 --> 00:15:05,860
I don't think I'd have managed 
to graduate without you.

273
00:15:06,370 --> 00:15:07,730
So Hitoma...

274
00:15:08,540 --> 00:15:09,890
Thank you.

275
00:15:10,280 --> 00:15:11,590
I should thank you, too.

276
00:15:12,090 --> 00:15:16,040
I learned a lot from being 
with you as well.

277
00:15:16,040 --> 00:15:17,220
Really?

278
00:15:17,220 --> 00:15:17,940
Yeah.

279
00:15:18,390 --> 00:15:20,440
A teacher does more than just teach.

280
00:15:20,910 --> 00:15:23,210
There's plenty we can learn 
from students, too.

281
00:15:24,460 --> 00:15:25,320
Not to mention...

282
00:15:25,940 --> 00:15:29,260
I have plenty of regrets as well.

283
00:15:30,370 --> 00:15:33,890
But I don't ever want to 
forget those regrets.

284
00:15:34,380 --> 00:15:37,190
Even though they're bad memories?

285
00:15:37,490 --> 00:15:40,480
Yeah. They're all precious to me.

286
00:15:40,830 --> 00:15:42,630
I won't forget them, either!

287
00:15:42,970 --> 00:15:45,530
Both the good and the bad!

288
00:15:46,040 --> 00:15:46,890
Glad to hear it.

289
00:15:46,890 --> 00:15:50,200
Take care even after I'm gone.

290
00:15:50,200 --> 00:15:52,370
Hitoma, Mirai.

291
00:15:52,670 --> 00:15:54,700
You too, Usami.

292
00:15:55,020 --> 00:15:57,540
Thank you. Take care.

293
00:15:57,950 --> 00:15:59,090
Until we meet again!

294
00:16:01,850 --> 00:16:03,380
Mr. Hitoma.

295
00:16:04,500 --> 00:16:05,340
What is it?

296
00:16:05,750 --> 00:16:07,190
Are they precious to you?

297
00:16:08,180 --> 00:16:09,100
What?

298
00:16:09,470 --> 00:16:12,200
Your regrets, I mean.

299
00:16:13,450 --> 00:16:16,850
I regret some things as well.

300
00:16:18,290 --> 00:16:19,340
Haruna.

301
00:16:21,700 --> 00:16:27,690
Back in high school, I wished 
I had never met you, Mr. Hitoma.

302
00:16:27,690 --> 00:16:29,580
And I still do.

303
00:16:29,580 --> 00:16:33,590
What I regret is having met you.

304
00:16:35,240 --> 00:16:38,930
Just now, you said you 
won't forget your regrets.

305
00:16:39,450 --> 00:16:40,260
I did.

306
00:16:41,690 --> 00:16:43,050
How awful.

307
00:16:43,580 --> 00:16:45,670
That's way too sad.

308
00:16:47,110 --> 00:16:51,670
I wish you'd forget all 
about what happened back then.

309
00:16:52,920 --> 00:16:54,220
I can imagine.

310
00:16:56,140 --> 00:16:57,470
But I won't forget.

311
00:16:58,700 --> 00:16:59,990
Why not?

312
00:17:02,650 --> 00:17:05,850
Even... Even though...

313
00:17:07,100 --> 00:17:08,690
I don't want that...

314
00:17:09,800 --> 00:17:10,510
Sorry.

315
00:17:10,510 --> 00:17:12,870
Stop! Don't apologize!

316
00:17:12,870 --> 00:17:15,870
I won't be able to live with myself!

317
00:17:18,650 --> 00:17:21,970
If you'd never gotten involved with me...

318
00:17:21,970 --> 00:17:25,210
You wouldn't have had to resign!

319
00:17:25,500 --> 00:17:27,490
What? Haruna?

320
00:17:27,980 --> 00:17:31,560
I didn't want to drag you into it, either!

321
00:17:31,560 --> 00:17:34,780
You love your job, don't you?

322
00:17:34,780 --> 00:17:36,820
Even I could tell that much!

323
00:17:42,770 --> 00:17:46,830
You still regret it, don't you?

324
00:17:48,060 --> 00:17:50,140
I told you to forget about it ...

325
00:17:50,630 --> 00:17:53,650
That you didn't need 
to let it bother you...

326
00:17:55,540 --> 00:17:58,870
Why? Stop it...

327
00:17:58,870 --> 00:18:04,310
I don't want to bring up 
painful memories for you.

328
00:18:06,010 --> 00:18:10,270
I don't want to be 
the cause of your regrets.

329
00:18:11,650 --> 00:18:15,930
I'm sorry, Mr. Hitoma...

330
00:18:21,050 --> 00:18:25,400
I apologize for letting 
you see me like that.

331
00:18:26,010 --> 00:18:31,320
I was sure you had a grudge against me.

332
00:18:31,550 --> 00:18:33,820
That would never be the case.

333
00:18:34,270 --> 00:18:36,840
If I did, I wouldn't have come here.

334
00:18:37,730 --> 00:18:40,280
Do you remember our last conversation?

335
00:18:41,630 --> 00:18:47,300
You blamed me for taking you seriously 
and trying to do the impossible.

336
00:18:48,050 --> 00:18:49,380
That's because...

337
00:18:50,840 --> 00:18:52,770
I wanted to hurt you.

338
00:18:54,470 --> 00:18:56,510
I lied to you on purpose.

339
00:18:56,510 --> 00:18:59,140
I knowingly said those nasty things.

340
00:18:59,800 --> 00:19:02,610
It wasn't me who came up 
with the physical discipline, either.

341
00:19:02,610 --> 00:19:05,130
I could never have done that.

342
00:19:05,690 --> 00:19:06,980
Was it Akazawa?

343
00:19:07,340 --> 00:19:09,360
Did Akazawa threaten you?

344
00:19:09,360 --> 00:19:10,440
No!

345
00:19:10,440 --> 00:19:13,390
What Rio did was really awful, but...

346
00:19:14,330 --> 00:19:16,220
The last part wasn't her.

347
00:19:17,500 --> 00:19:20,280
That was of my own volition.

348
00:19:21,170 --> 00:19:23,930
I've always regretted 
what I did back then.

349
00:19:25,100 --> 00:19:29,820
I hurt you, and 
I wanted to be hurt as well.

350
00:19:29,820 --> 00:19:32,700
Doing that would make you hate me.

351
00:19:33,160 --> 00:19:35,560
Once you hated me, I...

352
00:19:36,310 --> 00:19:38,630
thought I'd be free of the burden.

353
00:19:40,090 --> 00:19:43,410
But that's not what happened at all.

354
00:19:44,060 --> 00:19:46,410
At first, I felt a little better.

355
00:19:46,740 --> 00:19:48,670
I was glad you hated me.

356
00:19:49,640 --> 00:19:53,320
But I ended up hurting you.

357
00:19:54,220 --> 00:19:56,590
For my own temporary relief.

358
00:19:57,590 --> 00:20:00,860
When I thought of it like that, 
I started to feel so guilty...

359
00:20:02,460 --> 00:20:05,390
I'm so sorry.

360
00:20:09,970 --> 00:20:12,690
Maybe we're a little bit alike.

361
00:20:12,690 --> 00:20:13,840
What?

362
00:20:14,450 --> 00:20:16,120
It's not your fault, Haruna.

363
00:20:17,050 --> 00:20:21,050
I really am glad I never forgot about you.

364
00:20:22,930 --> 00:20:25,310
Why didn't you forget?

365
00:20:25,310 --> 00:20:28,670
I could never! You meant a lot to me.

366
00:20:28,670 --> 00:20:30,560
You said you regretted it.

367
00:20:30,560 --> 00:20:31,300
Yeah.

368
00:20:31,940 --> 00:20:36,780
I regret it, and I still wonder sometimes 
whether there was a better way.

369
00:20:37,810 --> 00:20:41,900
But I got to meet you again, 
and maybe that's enough.

370
00:20:42,790 --> 00:20:44,100
Seriously?

371
00:20:44,870 --> 00:20:47,620
Still, thank you.

372
00:20:48,180 --> 00:20:53,040
I'm glad to see you're still 
the same as well.

373
00:20:57,460 --> 00:21:01,990
I'll become a teacher just like you!

374
00:21:08,100 --> 00:21:10,350
Director's Office

375
00:21:09,230 --> 00:21:10,350
Mr. Hitoma.

376
00:21:10,680 --> 00:21:12,640
Well done surviving another year.

377
00:21:12,640 --> 00:21:17,560
The end of this year marks 
the end of your employment contract.

378
00:21:18,130 --> 00:21:23,230
The both of us would love 
to continue to keep you on.

379
00:21:23,230 --> 00:21:24,670
You said it.

380
00:21:24,670 --> 00:21:27,580
It's not easy finding 
humans who fit the bill.

381
00:21:27,580 --> 00:21:31,270
So, won't you renew your contract?

382
00:21:31,950 --> 00:21:35,710
I'd like to continue working here as well.

383
00:21:35,710 --> 00:21:38,860
I knew you'd see it that way!

384
00:21:38,860 --> 00:21:40,280
That's good to hear.

385
00:21:40,280 --> 00:21:44,140
There's still a lot more work 
I'd like to ask you to do.

386
00:21:44,460 --> 00:21:47,560
Actually, I've found a purpose now.

387
00:21:48,060 --> 00:21:50,220
Hm? What is it?

388
00:21:52,290 --> 00:21:54,650
Seeing through Tobari Haneda's graduation.

389
00:21:57,560 --> 00:22:00,960
Is that right? I hope you pull it off.

390
00:22:00,960 --> 00:22:01,610
Yeah.

391
00:22:03,580 --> 00:22:06,680
Hey, Mr. Hitoma. Do you like humans?

392
00:22:11,260 --> 00:22:14,630
Humans are annoying, 
they can't be honest...

393
00:22:16,500 --> 00:22:20,620
They lie all the time, 
and almost never stick to their claims.

394
00:22:21,220 --> 00:22:23,710
Their fickle natures cause me 
trouble to no end...

395
00:22:25,690 --> 00:22:29,450
But I'm content to live out my life 
at the mercy of their whims.

396
00:22:29,450 --> 00:22:31,180
In other words?

397
00:22:31,710 --> 00:22:33,130
I hate humans.

398
00:22:33,930 --> 00:22:37,630
Get involved in practically any way, 
and they cause you all sorts of trouble.

399
00:22:37,960 --> 00:22:38,730
But...

400
00:22:39,930 --> 00:22:45,150
That's the part of humans I'll hold 
dear as I continue to live with them.

401
00:22:46,610 --> 00:22:47,730
I see.

402
00:22:49,220 --> 00:22:52,540
